WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.830 --> 00:00:05.800
"She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" has an amazing
lead, the return of Professor Hulk, and some

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.919
surprising MCU connections.

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.280
So what do you need to know before the big
premiere?

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:12.400
Keep watching to find out.

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:18.340
At the D23 presentation in 2019, "Ms. Marvel,"
"Moon Knight," and "She-Hulk" were all announced

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:21.980
as upcoming series for Disney+ and Marvel
Studios.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.040
Almost three years later to the day, "She-Hulk:
Attorney at Law" is scheduled to drop on the

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.980
streamer on August 17, 2022.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.210
The series will follow the same format as
"WandaVision," running for a total of nine

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:38.540
shorter episodes as opposed to the MCU's other
shows with six one-hour-ish episodes.

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:40.400
New episodes will drop at 3 a.m.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.980
Eastern on Disney+ every Wednesday.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:47.270
If "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" follows the
once-per-week format, the series will conclude

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:49.520
with its finale on October 12.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.770
This puts the new show smack dab in the middle
of the release dates for "Thor: Love and Thunder"

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.330
and "Black Panther: Wakanda Forever."

00:00:57.330 --> 00:01:02.550
Joining the MCU in "She-Hulk: Attorney at
Law" is "Orphan Black" star Tatiana Maslany

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:05.300
as Jennifer Walters, aka She-Hulk.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:10.010
In December 2020, Marvel Studios revealed
the casting news on social media after Maslany

00:01:10.010 --> 00:01:12.790
denied her involvement just two months prior.

00:01:12.790 --> 00:01:17.190
The new series marks the first live-action
project for Maslany since her stint on HBO's

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:19.320
"Perry Mason" in 2020.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:23.660
Maslany spoke a little about her upcoming
role in "She-Hulk" while chatting with Empire

00:01:23.660 --> 00:01:24.660
magazine.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:28.630
The Canadian actress said part of her inspiration
for playing Jennifer came from the late Scottish

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.330
musician SOPHIE.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.330
She told Empire,

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:36.360
"What I love about SOPHIE's music is this
combo of organic and electrical, industrial-type

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.560
sounds that felt connected to She-Hulk."

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:43.250
When it comes to her character, the actress
called her story "the antithesis of most superhero

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:48.280
narratives," suggesting we're about to get
a whole new take on MCU heroes.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:53.810
The second original Avenger getting some time
in an MCU Disney+ series is Mark Ruffalo,

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:57.770
returning to the role of Bruce Banner after
his appearance in the post-credits of "Shang-Chi

00:01:57.770 --> 00:01:59.740
and the Legend of the Ten Rings."

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:04.551
Ruffalo's last major MCU role was in "Avengers:
Endgame," and it looks like "She-Hulk: Attorney

00:02:04.551 --> 00:02:07.460
at Law" might be his final performance with
the studio.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:11.640
Based on comments he made to Access Hollywood
at the "Adam Project" premiere, it's being

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.870
speculated that Ruffalo will retire from the
MCU.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:17.170
He had high praise for Maslany:

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:20.230
"Frickin' legendary as the She-Hulk.

00:02:20.230 --> 00:02:24.110
I'm passing the 'banner' onto her."

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:27.940
Based on what we see in the trailer for "She-Hulk,"
he'll serve as something of a Hulk coach to

00:02:27.940 --> 00:02:32.720
Jennifer Walters while she acclimates to her
newfound powers.

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:37.700
After almost a year of rumors, "The Good Place"
actress Jameela Jamil confirmed she was joining

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.980
the MCU in "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" in
her debut TikTok post.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:47.459
Jamil will play Titania , aka Mary MacPherran,
a longtime rival of She-Hulk.

00:02:47.459 --> 00:02:52.459
The comic book version of Mary gains her powers
from Doctor Doom after she is swept away into

00:02:52.459 --> 00:02:53.510
Battleworld.

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:57.590
She wields superhuman strength and is an expert
in hand-to-hand combat.

00:02:57.590 --> 00:03:01.800
She's quite the match for She-Hulk, but normally
finds herself the loser in their many battles.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:06.530
Since "The Good Place" concluded in 2020,
Jamil has been more selective about the projects

00:03:06.530 --> 00:03:07.590
she takes on.

00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:09.150
Jamil told Hollywood Life,

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:13.459
"I always want what I do to try and align
or embolden my social justice work.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:16.930
I feel like that is something that we are
achieving with this show — we're saying

00:03:16.930 --> 00:03:18.000
something important.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.660
We're doing something important, we're pushing
the boundaries."

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:26.600
When a new MCU project is on the horizon,
a frenzy begins online as fans try to figure

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.629
out if there will be any cameos.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:31.239
"She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" is no different.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:36.599
Only this time around, two cameos have already
been confirmed by Marvel Studios and Disney.

00:03:36.599 --> 00:03:41.130
After appearing in 2021's "Shang-Chi and the
Legend of the Ten Rings" for a brief fight

00:03:41.130 --> 00:03:44.069
scene, Abomination will return for "She-Hulk."

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:49.090
This time, we'll get to see him in his human
form, and Emil Blonsky, played by Tim Roth,

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.190
even makes an appearance in the trailer.

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:55.500
He's locked in a special cell, so we know
he's still not to be trusted 14 years after

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:57.099
his MCU introduction.

00:03:57.099 --> 00:03:59.550
"How do you feel?"

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:03.819
"Pissed off and ready for round three."

00:04:03.819 --> 00:04:08.290
Also joining "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" is
Wong, played by Benedict Wong, fresh off his

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:11.580
recent appearance in "Doctor Strange in the
Multiverse of Madness."

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:15.970
We haven't seen Wong yet in a trailer for
the show, but since he was the sorcerer fighting

00:04:15.970 --> 00:04:20.040
Abomination in "Shang-Chi and the Legend of
the Ten Rings," it makes sense that he would

00:04:20.040 --> 00:04:21.040
show up.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.780
There are plenty of other rumors suggesting
characters from all across the MCU will cameo,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:31.259
from Liv Tyler's return as Betty Ross to Krysten
Ritter reprising her role as Jessica Jones,

00:04:31.259 --> 00:04:34.680
but these should be taken with a grain of
salt.

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:38.850
The first official trailer for "She-Hulk:
Attorney at Law" shocked the MCU fandom by

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:41.180
giving them a brief glimpse of Frog-Man.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:46.469
A popular Twitter spoiler account had previously
leaked the character's inclusion in the series,

00:04:46.469 --> 00:04:48.949
but it wasn't taken too seriously at the time.

00:04:48.949 --> 00:04:53.569
No actor has been connected to Frog-Man, but
with Josh Segarra and Griffin Matthews attached

00:04:53.569 --> 00:04:57.999
to unknown characters, it's reasonably safe
to assume one of them is playing the obscure

00:04:57.999 --> 00:04:59.169
character.

00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:04.369
Not to be confused with his dad, the villainous
Leap-Frog, Frog-Man first appeared in 1982's

00:05:04.369 --> 00:05:06.039
"Marvel Team-Up #121."

00:05:06.039 --> 00:05:12.059
When Leap-Frog, real name Vincent Patilio,
gets arrested and put away, his son Eugene

00:05:12.059 --> 00:05:17.319
decides to use the mantle as a force for good
under the modified identity of Frog-Man.

00:05:17.319 --> 00:05:21.520
There is no substantial direct connection
between Jennifer Walters and Eugene in the

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:22.520
comics.

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:26.819
However, Leap-Frog's criminal endeavors frequently
pit him against Daredevil, and Matt Murdock

00:05:26.819 --> 00:05:32.339
just so happens to be a lawyer who recently
made his post-Netflix MCU debut in "Spider-Man:

00:05:32.339 --> 00:05:36.800
No Way Home," so that connection could explain
his appearance.

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:41.169
According to the official synopsis from Disney+,
"She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" will focus on

00:05:41.169 --> 00:05:46.020
Jennifer Walters, an attorney working at a
firm that deals with superhuman clients.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.939
Jennifer will also navigate a complicated
love life, which is depicted in the first

00:05:49.939 --> 00:05:51.370
trailer for the series.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:55.710
As she searches for dates, Jennifer will be
in her Hulk form, as it looks like the world

00:05:55.710 --> 00:05:57.949
has already accepted her new look.

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:02.319
As previously mentioned, Mark Ruffalo's Hulk
will teach Jennifer how to handle her new

00:06:02.319 --> 00:06:05.309
6-foot-7-inch form and superhuman strength.

00:06:05.309 --> 00:06:09.800
Everything looks fresh for Jennifer in "She-Hulk,"
as she is taking on a new job, new physique,

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:12.889
and new romantic interests all at the same
time.

00:06:12.889 --> 00:06:15.830
Not to mention her first opponent in Titania.

00:06:15.830 --> 00:06:19.490
There's a brief moment in the trailer where
the two women battle it out in a courtroom,

00:06:19.490 --> 00:06:23.669
but the root of their issues in this particular
series is still in the air.

00:06:23.669 --> 00:06:28.059
Much as the Hawkeye mantle was passed on to
Kate Bishop in "Hawkeye," we expect the same

00:06:28.059 --> 00:06:32.629
sort of thing to happen in "She-Hulk," with
Maslany being the MCU's primary green giant

00:06:32.629 --> 00:06:34.029
moving forward.

00:06:34.029 --> 00:06:35.029
"Yes!

00:06:35.029 --> 00:06:36.029
Yes!

00:06:36.029 --> 00:06:37.029
Yes!

00:06:37.029 --> 00:06:38.029
No!

00:06:38.029 --> 00:06:39.029
NO!"

00:06:39.029 --> 00:06:42.660
We all know by now how Bruce Banner gets his
powers, but the origin of She-Hulk's powers

00:06:42.660 --> 00:06:47.119
is a little more obscure, simply because the
character has spent comparatively little time

00:06:47.119 --> 00:06:48.710
in mainstream media.

00:06:48.710 --> 00:06:53.389
Unless you are a Marvel Comics reader, you
might be totally unaware of how Jennifer bulks

00:06:53.389 --> 00:06:54.389
up.

00:06:54.389 --> 00:06:58.159
Based on what we see in the trailer, we expect
to see Jennifer get her powers early in the

00:06:58.159 --> 00:06:59.159
series.

00:06:59.159 --> 00:07:02.490
It would be a surprise to find out she already
has them by the time the show begins, although

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.429
that's not impossible.

00:07:04.429 --> 00:07:09.039
Here's how it goes down: Jennifer is shot
by a man named Nicholas Trask who is seeking

00:07:09.039 --> 00:07:10.460
revenge against her father.

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:14.860
Her wounds are grave, and she needs a blood
transfusion, so her cousin Bruce steps up

00:07:14.860 --> 00:07:17.500
to help her out when there are no other options.

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:21.360
With gamma radiation coursing through his
veins, there was no way to avoid Jennifer

00:07:21.360 --> 00:07:24.210
getting the irradiated blood into her system.

00:07:24.210 --> 00:07:28.419
But it's not just Bruce's blood that turns
her; it's her anger and fear that really does

00:07:28.419 --> 00:07:29.419
the trick.

00:07:29.419 --> 00:07:33.050
"Those are like the baseline of any woman,
like, existing."

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.610
And just like that, she becomes superhuman.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:39.699
Jennifer is not quite as powerful as Bruce
in her Hulk form, and her stature is slightly

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:44.449
smaller, which makes her look more humanlike
and less monster-like.

00:07:44.449 --> 00:07:49.789
As with the three most recent Marvel Studios/Disney+
series, "She-Hulk: Attorney at Law" will have

00:07:49.789 --> 00:07:51.259
more than one director.

00:07:51.259 --> 00:07:55.189
"She-Hulk" will be split between Kat Coiro
and Anu Valia.

00:07:55.189 --> 00:07:59.889
Coiro has directed episodes of popular projects
like "Dead to Me" and "It's Always Sunny in

00:07:59.889 --> 00:08:04.749
Philadelphia," while Valia is known for her
work on "A.P. Bio" and the "Sex and the City"

00:08:04.749 --> 00:08:06.849
revival series "And Just Like That..."

00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:09.399
Coiro pushed hard to get the job, telling
Collider,

00:08:09.399 --> 00:08:14.719
"I'm a huge fan of the MCU, and I was actually
a giant fan of the She-Hulk comics, so when

00:08:14.719 --> 00:08:18.800
I heard they were making it, I went full court
press and really sold myself as the person

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:20.599
to bring this story to life.

00:08:20.599 --> 00:08:22.889
It was a huge and involved process."

00:08:22.889 --> 00:08:28.300
In an Instagram post from December 2020, Valia
revealed Coiro is taking the lead on "She-Hulk:

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:29.409
Attorney at Law," writing,

00:08:29.409 --> 00:08:33.800
"friggin stoked to go on this ride together
([Coiro] is our visionary leader im just doing

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:37.120
a few eppys !! but it'll be a fun one)."

00:08:37.120 --> 00:08:41.860
The Hollywood Reporter revealed that Jessica
Gao was hired as head writer for "She-Hulk:

00:08:41.860 --> 00:08:44.790
Attorney at Law" back in November 2019.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:49.280
Gao is an Emmy-winning writer who nabbed the
gold statue for her work on the "Rick and

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:50.640
Morty" episode "Pickle Rick."

00:08:50.640 --> 00:08:55.060
She also has writing credits on "Robot Chicken,"
"Big Time Rush," and "Silicon Valley," just

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:56.340
to name a few.

00:08:56.340 --> 00:09:00.890
Gao was absolutely flabbergasted to get the
job on "She-Hulk," and shared her excitement

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:04.080
in an Instagram post after the big news was
announced.

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:05.080
She wrote,

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.080
"DREAM COME TRUE.

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.080
I AM DECEASED.

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.310
(Don't worry, I will resurrect to do the job.)"

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:13.780
Subsequent social media posts of Gao's regarding
the new Disney+ series have only mirrored

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:15.220
her initial excitement.

00:09:15.220 --> 00:09:19.450
She shared casting news to her feed, and when
the first trailer was released, Gao also told

00:09:19.450 --> 00:09:25.090
the world on Instagram that she couldn't wait
for everyone to see Maslany in the role.

00:09:25.090 --> 00:09:29.190
We know for certain that "She-Hulk: Attorney
at Law" connects to "Shang-Chi and the Legend

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.870
of Ten Rings" in a minor way with a blink-and-you'll
miss it confirmation in the trailer.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:38.180
When we see Wong leaving the fight club in
the Phase 4 film, he opens a portal, and on

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:41.240
the other side is a room with a large cell
in the middle of it.

00:09:41.240 --> 00:09:45.320
The same cell can be seen in the "She-Hulk"
trailer, where Jennifer Walters talks to an

00:09:45.320 --> 00:09:47.370
imprisoned Emil Blonsky.

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:51.720
As far as future projects, it's possible we'll
see "She-Hulk" connect to the "Thunderbolts"

00:09:51.720 --> 00:09:54.300
movie recently declared as in-development.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:58.780
Some fans think Emil is being held in The
Cube — a SHIELD prison that houses various

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:03.090
super-powered criminals, occasionally of the
gamma-irradiated variety.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:08.200
All we're saying is if Valentina Allegra de
Fontaine needs someone to join a team already

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:13.260
consisting of John Walker and Yelena Belova,
she could probably swing by The Cube and offer

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.800
Emil a deal without much trouble.

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:20.890
Fans weren't too happy with the quality of
the CGI in the first "She-Hulk: Attorney at

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.180
Law" trailer, but that's not the only controversy
surrounding the series.

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:29.070
A few sources have come forward to say there
were some problems behind the scenes.

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:34.260
Former Variety and Collider writer Jeff Sneider
revealed in March 2022 on his "The Hot Mic

00:10:34.260 --> 00:10:38.440
with Jeff and John" podcast, that he's heard
about issues with "She-Hulk," claiming,

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:42.380
"I've heard not good things behind the scenes
... and I've asked whether it's 'Moon Knight'

00:10:42.380 --> 00:10:47.030
or 'Ms. Marvel' or 'Secret Invasion' or any
of these [projects], they are always like,

00:10:47.030 --> 00:10:48.860
'She-Hulk is the one that could be a problem."

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:53.440
Former Hollywood Reporter editor Matthew Belloni
mentioned in his website's newsletter in May

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.880
2022 that the newest Disney+ series are being
watched carefully, writing,

00:10:57.880 --> 00:11:03.040
"The upcoming 'She-Hulk' is supposedly a mess,
I've heard (even with Mark Ruffalo in a small

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:06.130
role), and 'Ms. Marvel' is another big test
for fans.

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:11.310
Nobody's saying Marvel's TV output is in trouble,
but it's something to keep an eye on."

